Using two different laptops to build a website is a recipe for disaster. I learned this the hard way last month.

I was bouncing between two machines to work on the site. Because a few changes hadn't been pushed to GitHub, the files on both laptops completely drifted out of sync.

In a desperate move to align them, I decided to just commit the entire root directory.

Big mistake. It completely trashed my local file system.

I spent the next two days doing absolutely nothing but untangling the mess. I eventually had to resort to zipping up the files and manually transferring them over. Two full days of zero development progress, all because of one impatient shortcut.

Lesson learned: Git is the source of truth for a reason. Trust the workflow, don't force it.

For those who bounce between multiple development machines, how do you keep your environments seamlessly in sync without losing your mind?

#WebDevelopment #SoftwareEngineering #Git #Programming #TechLessons
